fix(ui): F-0020 Dosing switch is drawn under forced colours in both states

Finding: F-0020 (P1, A11Y-22 forced colours).
Baseline: apply after F-0029.patch.

Contract
  Originating: under forced colours, the switch track and knob are visible, and on and off look different.
  Regression: journey switch-dosing-to-manual; axe, keyboard, contrast, layout, states, motion; no
  introduced finding.
  Scope: styles.css, a forced-colors media block for the switch only.
Drift class and layer: local defect; CSS only. The track and knob opt out of forced-colour adjustment and use
system colours: an outlined Canvas track with a ButtonText knob when off, and a Highlight track with a
HighlightText knob when on. The outline is inset, so the layout does not move.
Left alone: the switch outside forced colours, and its overshooting easing (F-0014/F-0018, P2 motion).
Re-test: run 20261006-160101-fix-f-0020.
  Probe 1 emulated forced colours at 1280 px and captured both states; the switch is drawn in each.
  Console: 0 errors. The journey passed (3/3). No finding was introduced. The 2 instances of F-0013 listed in the
  diff come from the F-0025 alarm chip.

